The function iterates through the input array, selects each element as the first element of a subarray, and recursively calls itself on the remaining elements. The function then adds the selected element to the beginning of each of these subarrays and adds all of these subarrays to the output.

The function terminates when the input array is empty, in which case it returns an array with a single empty array (representing the empty permutation).

