The key insight is to transform the problem into a standard "Climbing Stairs" problem, and then use the same dynamic programming approach. The optimized space is from the start to the end of the array, and the transition is computing the minimum cost of the current step based on the minimum cost of the previous two steps. At the end, we return the minimum cost of the last two steps, which is the answer to the original problem. The time complexity of this algorithm is O(N), the space complexity is O(N).

